message.content:
Below is a **complete, step‑by‑step playbook** you can follow (or adapt) to build a modern, production‑ready frontend for your e‑commerce site.  
It covers everything from the initial design phase to deployment, monitoring, and maintenance.  
Feel free to skip sections that already exist in your stack or replace them with your own tooling.

---

## 1. Planning & Requirements

| Item | Why it matters | How to do it |
|------|----------------|--------------|
| **Business goals** | Define what success looks like (conversion rate, load time, mobile share, etc.) | Create a KPI dashboard (Google Data Studio, Looker, etc.) |
| **Target audience** | Determines device mix, accessibility needs, and content strategy | User personas, market research |
| **Feature list** | Prioritises work and informs architecture | MoSCoW prioritisation, backlog grooming |
| **Tech constraints** | Avoids costly rewrites later | Existing backend, hosting provider, budget |
| **Compliance** | GDPR, PCI‑DSS, WCAG | Legal audit, privacy policy, cookie banner |

> **Tip:** Keep a living document (Google Docs, Notion, Confluence) that all stakeholders can view.

---

## 2. Wireframes & Prototypes

| Tool | Use case |
|------|----------|
| **Figma / Sketch / Adobe XD** | Low‑fidelity wireframes → High‑fidelity prototypes |
| **InVision / Marvel** | Interactive prototypes for stakeholder demos |
| **Storybook** | Component‑level design system preview |

### Checklist

- [ ] Navigation flow (desktop + mobile)
- [ ] Product listing page layout
- [ ] Product detail page (image gallery, description, reviews)
- [ ] Cart & checkout flow
- [ ] Account pages (login, register, order history)
- [ ] Error pages (404, 500)
- [ ] Accessibility annotations (WCAG 2.1 AA)

---

## 3. Tech Stack Decision

| Category | Options | Recommendation |
|----------|---------|----------------|
| **Framework** | React, Vue, Angular, Svelte | **React + Next.js** (SSR + SSG + API routes) |
| **Styling** | CSS Modules, Styled‑Components, Emotion, Tailwind CSS | **Tailwind CSS** (utility‑first + JIT) |
| **State Management** | Redux Toolkit, Zustand, Recoil, React Context | **Redux Toolkit** (for global cart, auth, etc.) |
| **Data Fetching** | SWR, React Query, Apollo Client | **React Query** (cache, background refetch) |
| **Type System** | JavaScript, TypeScript | **TypeScript** (type safety, IDE autocomplete) |
| **Testing** | Jest, React Testing Library, Cypress, Playwright | **Jest + RTL** (unit/integration) + **Cypress** (E2E) |
| **CI/CD** | GitHub Actions, GitLab CI, CircleCI | **GitHub Actions** (workflow per PR) |
| **Hosting** | Vercel, Netlify, AWS Amplify, Cloudflare Pages | **Vercel** (Next.js native) |
| **Analytics** | Google Analytics, Plausible, Segment | **Plausible** (privacy‑friendly) |
| **Error Tracking** | Sentry, LogRocket | **Sentry** (frontend + backend) |
| **Performance** | Lighthouse, WebPageTest | **Lighthouse** (CI badge) |

> **Why Next.js?**  
> - Built‑in SSR/SSG for SEO and fast first paint.  
> - API routes for serverless functions (e.g., payment webhook).  
> - Automatic code splitting and image optimisation (`next/image`).  

---

## 4. Project Skeleton

```bash
my-ecommerce/
├─ public/
│  ├─ assets/
│  └─ favicon.ico
├─ src/
│  ├─ components/
│  │  ├─ ui/          # UI primitives (Button, Card, Modal)
│  │  ├─ layout/      # Header, Footer, Sidebar
│  │  └─ pages/       # Page‑specific components
│  ├─ features/
│  │  ├─ cart/
│  │  ├─ auth/
│  │  └─ products/
│  ├─ hooks/
│  ├─ lib/
│  │  ├─ api.ts       # Axios instance + typed endpoints
│  │  └─ utils.ts
│  ├─ pages/
│  │  ├─ _app.tsx
│  │  ├─ index.tsx
│  │  ├─ product/[slug].tsx
│  │  ├─ cart.tsx
│  │  └─ api/
│  │     └─ stripe-webhook.ts   # Serverless function
│  ├─ store/
│  │  ├─ cartSlice.ts
│  │  ├─ authSlice.ts
│  │  └─ store.ts
│  ├─ styles/
│  │  ├─ globals.css
│  │  └─ tailwind.css
│  └─ types/
│     └─ index.d.ts
├─ .env.local
├─ .env.production
├─ .eslintrc.js
├─ .prettierrc
├─ jest.config.js
├─ next.config.js
├─ package.json
└─ README.md
```

> **Tip:** Keep `src/features` small and focused; each feature owns its own state slice, API calls, and UI components.

---

## 5. Core Components & Patterns

### 5.1 UI Primitives (Tailwind + React)

```tsx
// src/components/ui/Button.tsx
import { cva } from 'class-variance-authority';
import { forwardRef } from 'react';

const buttonVariants = cva(
  'inline-flex items-center justify-center rounded-md font-medium transition-colors focus:outline-none focus:ring-2 focus:ring-offset-2',
  {
    variants: {
      variant: {
        primary: 'bg-indigo-600 text-white hover:bg-indigo-700 focus:ring-indigo-500',
        secondary: 'bg-gray-200 text-gray-900 hover:bg-gray-300 focus:ring-gray-400',
      },
      size: {
        sm: 'px-3 py-1.5 text-sm',
        md: 'px-4 py-2 text-base',
        lg: 'px-5 py-3 text-lg',
      },
    },
    defaultVariants: {
      variant: 'primary',
      size: 'md',
    },
  }
);

export const Button = forwardRef<HTMLButtonElement, ButtonProps>(
  ({ className, variant, size, ...props }, ref) => (
    <button
      ref={ref}
      className={buttonVariants({ variant, size, className })}
      {...props}
    />
  )
);
Button.displayName = 'Button';
```

> **Why `class-variance-authority`?**  
> It gives you type‑safe variant handling while keeping Tailwind utilities.

### 5.2 Layout Components

```tsx
// src/components/layout/Header.tsx
import Link from 'next/link';
import { useSelector } from 'react-redux';
import { RootState } from '@/store/store';

export const Header = () => {
  const cartCount = useSelector((state: RootState) => state.cart.items.length);
  return (
    <header className="bg-white shadow">
      <nav className="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 flex justify-between h-16">
        <Link href="/">
          <a className="text-xl font-bold">Shop</a>
        </Link>
        <div className="flex space-x-4">
          <Link href="/cart">
            <a className="relative">
              Cart
              {cartCount > 0 && (
                <span className="absolute -top-2 -right-2 bg-red-600 text-xs rounded-full w-5 h-5 flex items-center justify-center text-white">
                  {cartCount}
                </span>
              )}
            </a>
          </Link>
          {/* Add auth links here */}
        </div>
      </nav>
    </header>
  );
};
```

### 5.3 Feature Slice (Redux Toolkit)

```ts
// src/store/cartSlice.ts
import { createSlice, PayloadAction } from '@reduxjs/toolkit';
import { Product } from '@/types';

interface CartState {
  items: Array<{ product: Product; quantity: number }>;
}

const initialState: CartState = { items: [] };

export const cartSlice = createSlice({
  name: 'cart',
  initialState,
  reducers: {
    addItem(state, action: PayloadAction<Product>) {
      const existing = state.items.find(i => i.product.id === action.payload.id);
      if (existing) {
        existing.quantity += 1;
      } else {
        state.items.push({ product: action.payload, quantity: 1 });
      }
    },
    removeItem(state, action: PayloadAction<string>) {
      state.items = state.items.filter(i => i.product.id !== action.payload);
    },
    clearCart(state) {
      state.items = [];
    },
  },
});

export const { addItem, removeItem, clearCart } = cartSlice.actions;
export default cartSlice.reducer;
```

### 5.4 API Layer (Axios + TypeScript)

```ts
// src/lib/api.ts
import axios from 'axios';

const api = axios.create({
  baseURL: process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL,
  headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
});

export const getProducts = async () => {
  const { data } = await api.get('/products');
  return data as Product[];
};

export const getProductBySlug = async (slug: string) => {
  const { data } = await api.get(`/products/${slug}`);
  return data as Product;
};
```

---

## 6. Routing & Data Fetching

### 6.1 Static Generation (SSG) for Product Pages

```tsx
// src/pages/product/[slug].tsx
import { GetStaticPaths, GetStaticProps } from 'next';
import { getProducts, getProductBySlug } from '@/lib/api';
import { Product } from '@/types';

export const getStaticPaths: GetStaticPaths = async () => {
  const products = await getProducts();
  const paths = products.map(p => ({ params: { slug: p.slug } }));
  return { paths, fallback: 'blocking' }; // fallback: true for incremental static regeneration
};

export const getStaticProps: GetStaticProps = async ({ params }) => {
  const product = await getProductBySlug(params?.slug as string);
  return { props: { product }, revalidate: 60 }; // revalidate every minute
};

export default function ProductPage({ product }: { product: Product }) {
  // Render product details
}
```

### 6.2 Client‑Side Data Fetching (React Query)

```tsx
// src/features/products/ProductList.tsx
import { useQuery } from '@tanstack/react-query';
import { getProducts } from '@/lib/api';

export const ProductList = () => {
  const { data, isLoading, error } = useQuery(['products'], getProducts);

  if (isLoading) return <p>Loading...</p>;
  if (error) return <p>Error loading products.</p>;

  return (
    <div className="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4 gap-6">
      {data.map(product => (
        <ProductCard key={product.id} product={product} />
      ))}
    </div>
  );
};
```

