## 11. CI/CD Pipeline (GitHub Actions)

```yaml
# .github/workflows/ci.yml
name: CI

on:
  pull_request:
    branches: [main]
  push:
    branches: [main]

jobs:
  build-test:
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    steps:
      - uses: actions/checkout@v4
      - uses: actions/setup-node@v4
        with:
          node-version: '20'
          cache: 'npm'
      - run: npm ci
      - run: npm run lint
      - run: npm run test -- --coverage
      - run: npm run build
      - uses: actions/upload-artifact@v4
        with:
          name: build
          path: .next
      - uses: actions/upload-artifact@v4
        with:
          name: coverage
          path: coverage
      - name: Lighthouse CI
        uses: treosh/lighthouse-ci-action@v9
        with:
          urls: https://example.com/
          outputPath: lighthouse-report.json
```

> **Deploy to Vercel**  
> Vercel automatically picks up the `build` artifact and deploys to preview environments on PRs.

---

## 12. Monitoring & Logging

| Tool | What it does | Integration |
|------|---------------|-------------|
| **Sentry** | Error tracking, performance monitoring | `@sentry/react`, `@sentry/node` |
| **LogRocket** | Session replay, debugging | `logrocket` SDK |
| **Datadog** | Infrastructure metrics | `next-datadog` |
| **Prometheus + Grafana** | Custom metrics | Exporter in API routes |

### Sentry Setup

```ts
// src/lib/sentry.ts
import * as Sentry from '@sentry/react';
import { Integrations } from '@sentry/tracing';

Sentry.init({
  dsn: process.env.SENTRY_DSN!,
  integrations: [new Integrations.BrowserTracing()],
  tracesSampleRate: 0.1,
});
```

Add this to `_app.tsx`:

```tsx
import '@/lib/sentry';
```

